{"content":[{"c":["TAMAR (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Wife of Er, the firstborn son of Judah by a Canaanitess. Later, as a widow, Tamar bore two sons to Judah named Perez and Zerah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.6-24","r":"Gen.38.6-24","rawR":"Gen.38.6-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.6-24","value":"Gen.38.6-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:6-24"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.4","r":"1Chr.2.4","rawR":"1Chr.2.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.4","value":"1Chr.2.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:4"},"). Tamar preserved the line of Judah through Perez (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.12","r":"Ruth.4.12","rawR":"Ruth.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.12","value":"Ruth.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 4:12"},"), and her name is recorded in the genealogy of Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.3","r":"Matt.1.3","rawR":"Matt.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.3","value":"Matt.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"GenealogyofJesusChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Genealogy of Jesus Christ"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Sister of Absalom and the daughter of David by his wife Maacah, the Geshurite. Through deceit, Tamar was seduced by Amnon, her half brother. In vengeance, Absalom, her full brother, had Amnon murdered at Baal-hazor (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.13.1-39","r":"2Sam.13.1-39","rawR":"2Sam.13.1-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.13.1-39","value":"2Sam.13.1-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.3.9","r":"1Chr.3.9","rawR":"1Chr.3.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.3.9","value":"1Chr.3.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 3:9"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Daughter of Absalom who was noted for her beauty (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.14.27","r":"2Sam.14.27","rawR":"2Sam.14.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.14.27","value":"2Sam.14.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 14:27"},"). She perhaps married Uriel of Gibeah and became the mother of Maacah. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MaacahMaachahPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MaacahMaachahPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MaacahMaachahPerson_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Maacah, Maachah (Person) #4"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"TamarPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 38:6-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.6-24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.6-24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.6-24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.4"},{"anchorText":"Ru 4:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.4.12","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.4.12","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.4.12"},{"anchorText":"Mt 1:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.1.3","rawQueryValue":"Matt.1.3","sourceRefExact":"Matt.1.3"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.13.1-39","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.13.1-39","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.13.1-39"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 3:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.3.9","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.3.9","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.3.9"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 14:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.14.27","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.14.27","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.14.27"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"79bd9dc445dbb23300f65aec4350640